      "text": "From the given information, we have $(x - \\frac{1}{x})^3 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 3(x - \\frac{1}{x})$.\nTherefore, $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} = (x - \\frac{1}{x})^3 + 3(x - \\frac{1}{x})$.\nSubstituting $x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4$, we get $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} = 4^3 + 3(4) = 64 + 12 = \\boxed{76}$.\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{76}.",
